; bfsodium SUBBYTES : every byte of the state through the AES S box
;
; NOTE square brackets are brainfuck loops  so comments use braces for counts;
;
; HAND WRITTEN; nothing is pasted INTO this file and this file cannot be
; pasted into anything  which is the point below;
;
; IO  in:  state{16}   (16 bytes)
;     out: state{16}   every byte replaced by its S box entry
;
; FIPS 197 section 5 point 1 point 1; The S box is the multiplicative inverse
; in GF(2^8) followed by an affine transform  and it is a CONSTANT: this file
; writes all 256 entries into the tape before it reads anything from them;
;
; THERE IS NO INTERFACE LINE AND THAT IS FORCED  not an oversight; The walk
; that index/fetch256 proved advances three cells per turn  so its loops are
; not pointer balanced  so tools/bffoot cannot bound a footprint for it and
; tools/bfexpand refuses to paste a file with no INTERFACE; So this is a
; PROGRAM; The walk is carried here rather than pasted  and an AES round will
; have to carry it too; That is the finding index/fetch256 recorded and this
; is the first file that has to live with it;
;
; THE STATE SITS BELOW THE FRAME AND THAT IS A MEASURED DECISION  not a
; layout preference; A byte moved over d cells costs about 2d per unit of
; itself  and a state parked ABOVE the table would sit seven hundred and
; seventy cells from the walker; BOTH FORMS WERE BUILT AND RUN on the same
; forty random states and they agree on every answer: this one averages 4
; million 197 thousand instructions and the other 10 million 642 thousand
; which is two and a half times  for nothing but travel; Below the frame the
; journey is at most seventeen cells and it disappears;
;
; AND THE TABLE IS BUILT ONCE AND READ SIXTEEN TIMES; that the table SURVIVES
; a read is index/fetch256twice's whole reason for existing  and it is what
; this file spends;
;
; THE TABLE IS NOT COMPUTED PER BYTE and the arithmetic says why; An inverse
; in the field is x to the 254  which is thirteen multiplies by square and
; multiply; A general multiply built from aes/xtime and idiom/xor8 is eight
; rounds of one of each  which on their MEASURED means is about 450 thousand
; instructions  so an inverse is near 6 million per byte against a fetch of
; 248 thousand; That is an estimate and not a measurement  because the general
; multiply is not written yet  but it is not close: the table is more than an
; order of magnitude cheaper and the 33 thousand instructions that write it
; are paid once for all sixteen bytes;
;
; TAPE MAP  (home @0)
;   @0x000:0x00f  state{16}  read here  and the answers come back here
;   @0x010:0x012  group 0  the walker's home; ITS TRAIL IS NEVER SET  which is
;                 what stops the walk back; the index arrives in its walker
;                 cell at @0x011 and the answer comes to rest there
;   @0x013:0x312  groups 1 to 256  the S box; element k in group k plus one
;                 with its datum at 19 plus 3k

; the state  and nothing else: the table is a constant and is
; written below rather than read
